1131	{"artifactId":"TASK-e6ddcdcb3d9cf330-s3-t1","entry":{"id":"00mvz5tdtj001-1492f7c0-d738-4861-ad18-968ef407e814","actor":{"id":"insrc:build","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-11-02T11:12:27.703Z","operation":"update","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"All four acceptance checks are backed by real, passing integration tests that exercise exactly what they claim (verified by reading ownership.test.ts, recovery.test.ts and the coordinator.ts/task-review-rpc.ts/router.ts/method-class.ts implementation they drive). Changes are centralized in task-review-rpc.ts's main-thread-only coordinator map, coordinator.ts's minimal storyWork/cleaning fence, and the router/method-class bypass set that s2's BUILD record explicitly deferred to S3 -- no new thread subsystem, worker-local coordinator copies, or persistent leases were introduced. Minor nit: two in-code comments (task-review-rpc.ts lines 20 and 61) still say integration \"remains S3\" even though this task is S3 completing it; cosmetic only, does not affect correctness.","data":{"kind":"build-round","round":{"testsPassed":true,"typecheckClean":true}}}}}
1204	{"artifactId":"TASK-e6ddcdcb3d9cf330-s3-t2","entry":{"id":"00mvz652ve002-2cf9131e-c0ce-4a30-ab9c-01ea2b5871e1","actor":{"id":"insrc:build","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-11-02T11:21:33.386Z","operation":"update","outcome":{"result":"fail","summary":"The two daemon-run named tests pass and most acceptance checks are genuinely met, but acceptance check 1 (registration/insrc_schema/guide/host agreement) is objectively broken: the task rewrote the insrc_code_review_step description and the steering-block.md code-review guide, and changed its registered phase list to CODE_REVIEW_PHASES, without updating the pre-existing lockstep regression guards (src/mcp/__tests__/schema-registry.test.ts EXPECTED_PHASES.insrc_code_review_step still literally reads ['start','judgements'], and src/mcp/__tests__/review-rule-text.test.ts still asserts the old `emit_judgements`/`confirm_wait`/controller-review wording that no longer appears anywhere). Those tests exist specifically to catch this exact drift and will fail the next time the mcp test subset or full sweep runs, so the task is not genuinely done.","data":{"kind":"build-round","round":{"testsPassed":true,"typecheckClean":true}}}}}
