1447	{"artifactId":"TASK-e6ddcdcb3d9cf330-s3-t3","entry":{"id":"00mvz6mnhh006-dfc2eb86-bb3c-44ca-af6f-f83604863811","actor":{"id":"insrc:build","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-11-02T11:35:13.253Z","operation":"update","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"Typecheck and the full cleanup.test.ts suite pass (5/5), and reading cleanup.ts, coordinator.ts, gates.ts, admission.ts, checkpoint.ts, record.ts and task-review-rpc.ts confirms the implementation genuinely does what each acceptance check and named test claims: cleanup is reached only through one shared post-approval hook used by direct/single/batch routes, validates every checkpoint against the durable CR via the reused prepareReviewAdmission/record validators (no second validator invented), is fenced against concurrent admission/execution/publication without blocking unrelated stories, and reports per-file deleted/retained/errors with idempotent, model-free retries. gates.ts delegates to the daemon via rpc('codeReview.task.cleanup',...) rather than importing daemon code directly, matching the 'injected delegation to owner, not daemon imports in workflow domain code' requirement. Changes are confined to the task-review/cleanup machinery, its tests, the gates.ts hook, and the daemon RPC/handler wiring — consistent with the Plan's own t3 description and dependencies (t1/t2).","data":{"kind":"build-round","round":{"testsPassed":true,"typecheckClean":true}}}}}
